2.1: App list with names (check this first)
data record(apmid = array($ClaimsApps))
| expand apmid
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.cloud_application_namespace
    | fields name = entity.name, tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter contains(tag, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
    | parse name, "LD '-' LD:nsName"
    | summarize nsName = takeFirst(nsName), by:{apmid}
  ], sourceField: apmid, lookupField: apmid, prefix: "n."
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:") or startsWith(tag, "APPName:")
    | summarize ids = collectDistinct(if(startsWith(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1])),
                names = collectDistinct(if(startsWith(tag, "APPName:"), splitString(tag, "APPName:")[1])),
                by:{tagSet = toString(tags)}
    | filter arraySize(ids) == 1
    | fieldsAdd apmid = ids[0], hostName = names[0]
    | summarize hostName = takeFirst(hostName), by:{apmid}
  ], sourceField: apmid, lookupField: apmid, prefix: "h."
| fieldsAdd appName = coalesce(n.nsName, h.hostName, apmid)
| fields apmid, appName
| sort appName asc


Check: 59 rows, and the 6 host-only apps (Blue Squared, BC Benefit Determination, and so on) show a name rather than an APMID.

2.2: Host availability per app
timeseries cpu = avg(dt.host.cpu.usage), by:{dt.entity.host}, from:-30m
| fieldsAdd up = isNotNull(arrayLast(cpu))
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields id, tags
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter contains(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize hostsReporting = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.host),
            hostsUp = countDistinctExact(if(up, dt.entity.host)),
            by:{apmid}


Check: this only counts hosts that sent at least one data point in the last 30 minutes. A host that went down over an hour ago won't show up here at all. If you see that happening, tell me and I'll switch the total to come from dt.entity.host.

2.3: Service failure rate per app
timeseries {req = sum(dt.service.request.count), fail = sum(dt.service.request.failure_count)},
           by:{dt.entity.service}, from:-1h
| fieldsAdd req = arraySum(req), fail = arraySum(fail)
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.service
    | fields id, tags
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.service, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter contains(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize services = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.service),
            requests = sum(req), failures = sum(fail), by:{apmid}
| fieldsAdd failRatePct = if(requests > 0, round(100.0 * failures / requests, decimals:2), else: 0.0)
| sort failRatePct desc


Check: if dt.service.request.failure_count gives an error, run fetch metric.series | filter contains(metric.key, "dt.service.request") | summarize count(), by:{metric.key} and send me the keys.

2.4: Container health per app

Namespaces are named app<APMID>-…, so the APMID can be read straight from the namespace name. The first 11 characters (app00005029) give it.

timeseries restarts = sum(dt.kubernetes.container.restarts), by:{k8s.namespace.name}, from:-1h
| fieldsAdd restarts = arraySum(restarts)
| filter startsWith(k8s.namespace.name, "app")
| fieldsAdd apmid = upper(substring(k8s.namespace.name, from:0, to:11))
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize namespaces = countDistinctExact(k8s.namespace.name),
            restarts1h = sum(restarts), by:{apmid}
| sort restarts1h desc


Check: Q5 earlier listed the metric as container.restarts. I haven't confirmed the full key name. If this returns nothing, run fetch metric.series | filter contains(metric.key, "restart") | summarize count(), by:{metric.key}.

2.5: Active problems per app
fetch dt.davis.problems, from:-30d
| sort timestamp desc
| dedup display_id
| filter event.status == "ACTIVE" and dt.davis.is_duplicate == false
| expand tag = entity_tags
| filter contains(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize activeProblems = countDistinctExact(display_id),
            categories = collectDistinct(event.category),
            oldestStart = min(event.start),
            by:{apmid}
| fieldsAdd hasAvailability = contains(toString(categories), "AVAILABILITY")


